  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application as submitted relates to the conversion of a\r\nC3(a) dwelling to a residential care home for children (Use Class C2).\r\nTherefore, the prerequisites are that the proposal must meet an identified need, be\r\nof high-quality design and be located in areas that have the facilities the\r\nresidents require and be located close to public transport. Due to\r\ninsufficient information the principle of development in relation to Policy 21\r\n(Supported and Specialist Accommodation) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024)\r\ncould not be established.",
    "In the absence of proposed plans which illustrate the nature\r\nof the proposed works at ground floor and within the loft space it cannot be\r\nconfirmed that the development would be consistent with Policy 53 (Urban\r\nDesign) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024).&nbsp;",
    "In the absence of proposed plans which\r\nillustrate the nature of the proposed works at ground floor and within the loft\r\nspace, a true assessment with regard to neighbouring amenity impacts could not\r\nbe made in relation to Policy 57 (Amenity) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan\r\n(2024",
    "The proposed development, fails to make adequate provision\r\nfor the secure storage of 2No. bicycles (long stay) and 1No. bicycle (short\r\nstay), contrary to Policy T5 of the London Plan, Policy 61&nbsp;and Appendix 1\r\n– Parking standards of the Waltham Forest&nbsp;Local Plan (2024) and London\r\nCycle Design Standards (2014)."
  ],
